# Commercial or organizational use requires a written license.
# Contact: warith@digi77.com
#
# Description:
# The window that replaces three terminal launchers:
#
#     xfce4-terminal -e /usr/local/bin/kodachi-system-update
#     xfce4-terminal -e /usr/local/bin/kodachi-binary-install
#     xfce4-terminal -e /usr/local/bin/kodachi-deps-install
#
# WHY THEY ARE BEING REPLACED, and why only on Debian family. The binary one
# runs the TARBALL PACK installer, which downloads a signed pack from
# kodachi.cloud and unpacks it into /opt/kodachi/dashboard/hooks. That is the
# right and only mechanism on Fedora, Arch and anything else with no apt, and it
# stays exactly where it is. On Kodachi itself the same binaries arrive as
# signed .deb packages from the real repository, so running the pack installer
# here means two package managers owning the same files, and the one that runs
# second wins silently. The deps installer is the same story: apt already
# resolves those ~150 packages as declared dependencies.
#
# What this window may NOT do, deliberately:
#   - it never runs apt itself. Every privileged action goes through
#     kodachi-repo-apt under pkexec, which takes a closed verb set and builds
#     each apt invocation from constants. A sudoers NOPASSWD rule was considered
#     and rejected: it would be a new passwordless root grant for every member
#     of %sudo, where pkexec asks for the password the same way the shipped
#     Synaptic cell already does. (That cell's payload is `pkexec
#     /usr/sbin/synaptic` as of G92, 2026-08-23: pkexec resolves a bare name
#     against the CALLER's PATH and the graphical session has no /usr/sbin, so
#     the bare form silently did nothing. The auth model this paragraph is
#     about did not change.)
#   - it never shows a version, hash or date it did not read from an apt index
#     or an HTTP header. See kodachi_repo, which returns None rather than a
#     plausible value, and the window prints the absence in words.
#
# KODACHI_DRY_RUN=1 prints the privileged command instead of running it.

