# THE SIDEBAR, as the approved mockup draws it: three headed groups, each row
# carrying its own count on the right. The shared shell's _add_nav puts the
# same window icon on every row, which is what "icons are boring" was about,
# so these rows are built here instead and carry a per-row glyph.
#
# `kind` says what a click does, and it is not the same for every row:
#   channel  , switch the table to that Kodachi channel
#   filter   , narrow the table inside the current channel
#   page     , switch the whole stack to another destination
#
# THERE IS NO `legacy` KIND ANY MORE. The rail carried a LEGACY group with the
# three terminal scripts this window replaces, on the reasoning that the apt
# repository is Debian-only and the bash pack installer is still the only route
# onto Fedora or Arch. The operator removed it on sight, 2026-08-21, from the
# annotated a3.png: "we dont need the legacy stufff here remove them". He is
# right about this window: it manages an apt repository, and a machine with no
# apt repository cannot use anything else on this rail either, so the group was
# three dead rows on every machine that could actually open it. The scripts
# themselves are untouched at /usr/local/bin and remain the documented route
# for a non-Debian install.
SIDEBAR = [
