# three-line stanza into /etc/apt/auth.conf.d/kodachi-dev.conf that the ISO
# hook and the acceptance harness already write, reading both fields from
# STDIN so neither ever reaches argv, and the button below collects them.
# ONE DEFINITION, IN THE DATA LAYER. The path used to be declared here and
# nowhere else, which was fine while only the window cared about it. It is not
# fine now that `repo.catalog()` gates the dev LISTING on the same file: two
# copies of a security-relevant path in two modules is a drift waiting to
# happen, and the drift would be silent in the permissive direction (the
# library thinks the machine is not entitled and hides the channel, or worse,
# the window thinks it is).
DEV_AUTH_FILE = repo.DEV_AUTH_FILE
